      "note": "Runs on Magnific (Freepik's API, api.magnific.com) with the Magnific key; every API call costs credits, whatever the web plan says; not run against the live API yet. The pictures go inline (base64) to Magnific / Freepik (Freepik Company S.L., Málaga, Spain), which hosts inputs and outputs on its own or its providers' platforms, uses them for security and to improve its products and not to train its own models; the docs do not say where the model runs. Instruction edit of the crop plus the reference layers, no mask input: the stitch keeps the selection. For area-directed edits set Fill to green and Original on, and say \"fill the green area\". GPT Image 2 on Magnific renders ten preset shapes only: the crop's context is widened to the nearest one the picture can give, so the answer lines up with it (a crop that cannot be widened is centre-cropped). Resolution is the answer's tier. At most sixteen pictures, 20 MiB each and 64 MiB together. No transparent background on this route (opaque or auto only). Magnific's price list gives no EUR price; an edit is billed by quality alone."
